      "kind": "problem",
      "theorem_name": "OAI.PiExponent.DeterminantContradiction.no_fixed_data_of_interpolation_and_analytic_aggregate",
      "theorem_title": "The interpolation and analytic bounds exclude fixed admissible data",
      "formal_statement": "theorem OAI.PiExponent.DeterminantContradiction.no_fixed_data_of_interpolation_and_analytic_aggregate\r\n    (hgeometry : GlobalInterpolationStatement) (hanalytic : AnalyticAggregateStatement)\r\n    (nu : ℝ) (hnu : 2 < nu) (d : FixedData nu) : False := by\r\n  sorry\r\n",
      "natural_language_statement": "Assume the original global interpolation statement and analytic aggregate statement. For every real exponent $\\nu>2$ and every fixed admissible datum $d:\\mathrm{FixedData}(\\nu)$, these hypotheses imply a contradiction:\n\n$$\n\\mathrm{GlobalInterpolation}\\;\\land\\;\\mathrm{AnalyticAggregate}\\;\\Longrightarrow\\;\\bot.\n$$\n\nThus no fixed admissible family can coexist with both source hypotheses at an exponent above $2$.  This is the source theorem that converts the determinant estimates into the conditional lower bound for rational approximations to $\\pi$.",
      "definitions": "import Definitions.Def_OAI_PiExponent_ApproximationDefinitions\nimport Definitions.Def_OAI_NumberTheory_PiExponent_Approximation_DeterminantContradiction_CoreData\n\nopen OAI.PiExponent OAI.PiExponent.DeterminantContradiction\n\n",
